# Access Control Plan
## Restaurant Online Ordering and Table Reservation System

### 1. Purpose
The purpose of this access control plan is to protect the restaurant database by assigning appropriate permissions to different users.

### 2. User Roles

| Role | Description |
|---|---|
| Admin | Manages the database and has full access to system records. |
| Staff | Handles customer orders and table reservations. |
| Customer | Accesses menu information and submits orders and reservations. |

### 3. Access Permissions

| Database Operation | Admin | Staff | Customer |
|---|---|---|---|
| View Menu | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| Manage Menu | Yes | No | No |
| View Orders | Yes | Yes | No |
| Update Orders | Yes | Yes | No |
| Create Orders | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| View Reservations | Yes | Yes | No |
| Manage Reservations | Yes | Yes | No |
| Create Reservations | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| Delete Records | Yes | No | No |

### 4. Security Measures
- Apply role-based access control.
- Give users only the permissions required for their responsibilities.
- Restrict unauthorized database operations.
- Protect database credentials.
- Regularly review user permissions.

### 5. Expected Result
The implementation should prevent unauthorized database access and ensure that each role can only perform its assigned operations.